t, to 97.45 dollars a barrel at the low point.\nIran has halted message exchanges with the United States via mediation in protest against Israel's actions in Lebanon, Iran's semi-official Tasnim news agency reported Monday.\n![](http://www.chinaview.cn/20260602/09c3a8d5ef1048e6bff0ecd843f819b1/2026060209c3a8d5ef1048e6bff0ecd843f819b1_XxjidwE000003_20260602_CBMFN0A003.JPG)\nIsrael orders military to strike Beirut's southern suburbs\nIsraeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and Defense Minister Israel Katz on Monday said in a joint statement that they had ordered the military to strike Beirut's southern suburbs.\nAccording to the statement, the order was given following repeated Hezbollah violations of the ceasefire in Lebanon, including rocket and drone attacks targeting northern Israeli cities.\nIsrael's Channel 12 News reported that the move came after the United States approved Israel's requests to expand military activity in Lebanon, shifting from an initial focus on the country's south to include airstrikes in the capital city.\n![](http://www.chinaview.cn/20260602/09c3a8d5ef1048e6bff0ecd843f819b1/2026060209c3a8d5ef1048e6bff0ecd843f819b1_XxjidwE000003_20260602_CBMFN0A004.JPG)\nEthiopians head to polls in 7th general election\nPolling stations opened across Ethiopia on Monday morning as millions of voters are set to cast their ballots in the country's seventh general election.\nAccording to the National Election Board of Ethiopia, more than 54 million Ethiopians have registered to vote. Voters will elect representatives to the House of Peoples' Representatives, the lower chamber of parliament, as well as members of regional councils.\nElection authorities said that more than 10,000 candidates from 42 political parties, along with several independent candidates, are contesting seats in both the House and regional legislatures.\n![](http://www.chinaview.cn/20260602/09c3a8d5ef1048e6bff0ecd843f819b1/2026060209c3a8d5ef1048e6bff0ecd843f819b1_XxjidwE000003_20260602_CBMFN0A001.JPG)\nU.S., Iran exchange strikes amid ongoing peace efforts\nU.S. Central Command said on Sunday that the U.S. military conducted \"self-defense strikes\" on Iranian radar and command as well as control sites for drones in parts of Iran over the weekend.\nThe strikes occurred on Saturday and Sunday in response to \"aggressive Iranian actions that included the shootdown of a U.S. MQ-1 drone that was operating over international waters,\" the command said on X.\n\"U.S. fighter aircraft swiftly responded by eliminating Iranian air defenses, a ground control station, and two one-way attack drones that posed clear threats to ships transiting regional waters,\" it added.\n■\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：2026年6月2日 国际市场 重大消息\n\n网页标题：今日国际国内财经新闻精华摘要|2026年6月2日|以色列|停火|内塔尼亚胡|特朗普|黎巴嫩_手机网易网\n\n网页链接：http://m.163.com/dy/article/KUDEI8F905568W0A.html\n\n发布时间：2026-06-02T08:01:00+08:00\n\n网页内容：今日国际国内财经新闻精华摘要｜2026年6月2日\n新浪财经\n2026-06-02 08:01\n来源：芝麻AI\n一、国际新闻\n当地时间6月1日，美国总统特朗普在多个场合表示，预计将在“未来一周内”与伊朗达成谅解备忘录，以延长当前停火安排并重新开放霍尔木兹海峡，谈判虽出现“小插曲”但已解决，目前仍有几个点待敲定[1][2][3]。\n他同时称，以色列与黎巴嫩真主党已同意停止一切交火，美方不会向贝鲁特派遣军队，所有驰援部队均已撤回[4][5]。\n以色列 总理内塔尼亚胡则通过社交媒体证实，与特朗普通电话时明确表示，若真主党继续袭击以色列城市和民众，以方将对贝鲁特相关目标实施打击，国防军将按计划在黎巴嫩南部行动[6][7]。\n黎巴嫩总统办公室随后发表声明，确认真主党已承诺停止对以打击[8]。\n伊朗外交部则发表声明，指出美国对违反伊美停火协议及以色列违反黎以停火协议负有直接责任，伊朗将在必要时捍卫自身利益[9][10][11]。\n能源市场方面，美国能源部数据显示，上周战略石油储备减少800万桶原油，此前两周分别减少910万桶和创纪录的990万桶，当前库存降至3.571亿桶，为2024年1月以来最低水平[12][13]。\n受相关局势影响，WTI原油突破93美元/桶，日内涨0.31%[14]。\n此外，三位消息人士称，OPEC+很可能在周日会议上将7月石油产量配额每日上调18.8万桶[15]。\n金融市场方面，美股三大股指集体收涨，道指涨0.09%，标普500指数涨0.27%，纳指涨0.41%；英伟达股价收盘上涨6.3%，市值增加3190亿美元，“七姐妹”中微软涨2.31%，谷歌、苹果等多股下跌[16]。\n纳斯达克中国金龙指数收涨1.46%，海天网络涨339.83%，声网涨16.22%[17]。\n现货白银突破75美元/盎司，日内涨0.08%[18]；比特币则跌破71000美元，日内跌3.69%[19]。\n芝商所启动加密货币期货和期权全天候交易[20]。\n企业动态方面，谷歌母公司Alphabet拟通过股权融资筹集800亿美元，包括300亿美元承销发行、400亿美元按市价发行及伯克希尔100亿美元私募配售，资金将用于扩建AI算力基础设施[21][22][23][24]。\n计算设备制造商龙头慧与科技（HPE）股价盘后大涨超35%，公司预计未来18个月服务器需求将推动强劲增长[25]。\nAnthropic已向SEC秘密提交IPO注册文件草案，力争最快于今年秋季登陆美股[26][27]。\nSpaceX提交的S-1文件修正案显示，马斯克已接受为期366天的锁定期，未经高盛同意不得出售股份[28][29]。\n亚马逊宣布GPT-5.5、GPT-5.4及Codex等OpenAI模型现已接入亚马逊Bedrock平台[30]。\n联合太平洋高管私下否认与特朗普就收购15%股权进行谈判[31]。\n其他方面，日本自民党拟出台加密货币ETF相关法律框架，并推动锚定日元的稳定币落地[32]。\n德国地学研究中心（GFZ）报告意大利南部发生6.55级地震[33]。\n佛罗里达州总检察长就人工智能相关损害起诉OpenAI[34]，市场消息称微软即将发布全新人工智能模型并推出Windows系统优化升级[35]。\n二、国内新闻\n市场方面，液化石油气连续主力合约日内涨5%，现报5834.00元[36]；低硫燃料油连续主力合约日内同样涨5%，现报4878.00元[37]。\n企业动态方面，智谱在港交所公告称，董事会会议已通过建议向中国相关监管机构申请配发及发行A股，并在上海证券交易所科创板上市，发行数量占发行后总股本的2%至8%（不含超额配股权），相关决议案将提交年度股东会批准[38]。\n\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：2026年6月2日 国际市场 重大消息\n\n网页标题：GLOBAL MARKETS-Stocks bounce as AI optimism offsets Middle East anxiety\n\n网页链接：https://www.lse.co.uk/news/global-markets-stocks-bounce-as-ai-optimism-offsets-middle-east-anxiety-n8ml9jsd7vggf0e.html\n\n发布时间：2026-06-02T10:37:00+08:00\n\n网页内容：GLOBAL MARKETS-Stocks bounce as AI optimism offsets Middle East anxiety\nTue, 02nd Jun 2026 10:37\n![](https://static.lse.co.uk/news/medium/global-markets-stocks-bounce-as-ai-optimism-offsets-middle-east-anxiety-n8ml9jsd7vggf0e.jpg)\n* AI optimism and strong tech forecasts drive global stock rally\n* Oil slips, but Middle East tensions ⁠persist\n* Euro zone core inflation rises, ECB rate hike expected (Updates throughout)\nLONDON, June 2 (Reuters) - Global stocks rallied on Tuesday, buoyed by fresh AI optimism after Anthropic moved towards a U.S. stock market listing, while oil prices ‌and bond yields fell on renewed hopes of a U.S.-Iran deal.\nBrent crude futures dropped more than 1% to $94 a barrel, paring the previous session's sharp gains, ⁠after U.S. President Donald Trump said talks with Iran were ongoing.\nHis comments came ⁠despite a report that Tehran had suspended indirect negotiations with Washington to end hostilities, keeping investors cautious about efforts to end the three-month war and underlining the fragility of an ongoing ceasefire.\nEurope's STOXX 600 was up nearly 0.8% in morning trading, as a strong forecast from chipmaker STMicroelectronics lifted technology stocks.\nAI ENTHUSIASM\nAnthropic said on Monday it had confidentially filed ‌for a U.S. initial public offering, edging ahead of rival OpenAI in a closely watched race to reach public markets. Google parent Alphabet is also seeking to raise $80 billion in equity to fund the expansion of its AI infrastructure.\n\"This speaks to the huge sums involved in keeping pace in the AI arms race. It represents a significant shift from a period of bumper free cash flow to going cap in hand to the markets to help fund its expansion,\" Russ Mould, investment director at AJ Bell, said.\nOn the macro front, the Institute for ‌Supply Management on Monday said U.S. manufacturing PMI rose to 54.0 in May from 52.7 the previous month, beating expectations to hit a four-year high, likely driven by firms front-loading orders amid ‌rising prices and supply concerns linked to the Iran war.\nFutures on the S\u0026P 500 and Nasdaq 100 were down around 0.1%, pointing to a slightly weaker open after both indexes posted an eighth straight gain and fresh record highs on Monday .\n\"That marks the first time in a year the S\u0026P has achieved eight consecutive daily gains. And if you look at the moves on a weekly basis, a positive gain this week would ‌be the S\u0026P’s 10th consecutive advance, which is something we haven’t seen since 1985,\" Deutsche Bank strategist Jim Reid said.\nIn Taipei, Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang said the company has enough supply to support strong growth in central processing units (CPUs) and graphics processing units (GPUs), but acknowledged supply constraints remain a ⁠concern.\nSouth Korean ⁠equities were volatile, with the benchmark KOSPI swinging sharply lower after hitting a record high ‌as bellwethers like Samsung Electronics and SK Hynix seesawed.\nIn currency markets, the dollar was broadly steady. The euro , still 1.5% below its level at the start of the war, was last at $1.1643.\nData showed euro zone core inflation rose 2.5% year-on-year in May, above expectations of 2.4% and April's 2.1%. Money markets ‌price in a quarter-point European Central Bank rate hike this month, with at least one more by year-end.\nIn bonds, the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield fell 4.4 basis points to 4.43%, while Germany's 10-year Bund yield dropped nearly 6 bps to 2.956%.\nGold rose 1% to $4,527 an ounce. (Additional reporting by Gregor Stuart Hunter in Singapore. Editing by Stephen Coates and Mark Potter)\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：2026年6月2日 国际市场 重大消息\n\n网页标题：大河财立方发布“立方风控鸟·早报”\n\n网页链接：https://www.coze.cn/share-article/201780357944112640\n\n发布时间：2026-06-02T08:02:35\n\n网页内容：# 6月2日财经早报：城投发债、公司易主终止、摘帽、减持等动态密集释放许昌市城投发展集团获批注册8亿元中期票据。和仁科技终止筹划控制权变更事项，公司股票于2026年6月2日起复牌。*ST荣控股票交易将于2026年6月3日起撤销退市风险警示，证券简称变更为“荣丰控股”；*ST交投股票交易将于2026年6月3日起撤销退市风险警示及其他风险警示，证券简称变更为“交投生态”。铂科新材拟发行H股并在港交所主\n"}